    <section><h2>3. What Kindling provides</h2><p>Kindling helps you select travel media, arrange it into editable memory trails, add private context, search and revisit those trails, and create sharing artifacts. It is not a travel booking, navigation, public social, archival-backup, medical, or emergency service.</p><p>Automatic grouping and place suggestions may be incomplete or wrong. You remain in control of edits, privacy selections, and what you share.</p></section>
    <section id="pro"><h2>4. Kindling Pro</h2><p>The first two saved trips are free. Pro unlocks unlimited trails, premium sharing themes, branding controls, and expanded resurfacing controls. Kindling may offer monthly and annual subscriptions and a one-time Lifetime purchase. The App Store displays current price, billing period, and trial eligibility.</p><p>Lifetime is a non-expiring entitlement to Pro features included in this Kindling app during its supported life. It does not promise that the app, every feature, third-party service, or compatibility with future systems will exist forever, and it does not include separately sold successor products.</p></section>
    <section id="billing"><h2>5. Billing, renewal, cancellation, restoration, and refunds</h2><p>Apple processes all purchases. Subscriptions renew automatically until canceled through your Apple Account. Cancellation stops future renewal; access normally continues through the paid period. Restore purchases asks Apple for entitlements associated with the same Apple Account.</p><p>Apple controls App Store refunds. Request one through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/" rel="external">reportaproblem.apple.com</a> or Apple Support.</p></section>
    <section><h2>6. Your content</h2><p>You keep your rights in selected media, notes, recordings, tags, and other content. You are responsible for having permission to use and share it. Kindling does not claim ownership of your memories or use them to train AI models.</p></section>
